a unlv medical student saves a life on  her way to watch the raiders at  allegiant stadium sounds like something  from a movie but it actually happened  thanks for joining us i'm denise  baldesque and i'm brian loftis a man was  hit by a car on his way to a preseason  game last month and if it weren't for  this heroic action his story could have  ended a whole lot differently sasha  loftus joins us live near valley view  and russell with a story you will only  see on 8 news now  denise and brian this is the exact spot  where that man was hit by a car you can  see the car smashed into him and what  used to be a light pole where that cone  is now luckily liz grosbeck was here at  just the right time to make sure he made  it  this gruesome scene marked the start of  the raiders preseason last month a man  hit and seriously hurt by a car near  allegiant stadium causing sheer panic  and chaos we heard one just screaming  that's when emt certified unlv medical  student liz grosbeck who was on her way  to the game jumped into action i was  really hoping he was going to survive  she says the man who was missing a limb  and had serious injuries to his face  needed help until an ambulance arrived  so she did her best to stop the bleeding  and made sure he could breathe i just  really was hoping we could get ems there  as quickly as possible get him to a  hospital thanks to her quick thinking  and solid training he did survive but if  you call grossbeck a hero she'll smile  and say she just did what she could to  help another human being not so much of  a  like i saved a life it's more thank god  that guy survived and she's grateful the  stars aligned to put her skills to use  at exactly the right time everything  happened to end up just right so that  this incredibly unlucky situation could  be as lucky as possible  you can see still quite a bit of debris  as well at this spot where this crash  happened about a month ago the man who  was hit was just released from the  hospital we're told now police say the  driver responsible for this crash did  leave the scene on foot police are still  searching for that suspect if you have  any information call metro police or  crime stoppers reporting live in las  vegas tonight sasha loftis 8 news now
 

